The function is a single forwarding call to the base-class setter with no redundant work; there is nothing to hoist or reorder, so the fastest correct drop-in is the same code (already implicitly inline within the class).

```cpp
    void SetAwakeningsCount(FIT_UINT8 awakeningsCount)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(11, awakeningsCount, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```